==English==
[[File:Ponticola ratan, Gulf of Odessa, Ukraine - 20110620-01.jpg|thumb|A Ratan goby (''[[w:Ponticola ratan|Ponticola ratan]]'') from the [[w:Gulf of Odessa|Gulf of Odessa]], [[w:Ukraine|Ukraine]]]]
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|la|gobius||gudgeon}}, from {{uder|en|grc|κωβιός|}}, a type of small fish, of unknown ultimate origin. See also {{l|en|gudgeon}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɡəʊbi/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-goby.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|goby|+}}

# Any of various small fish from the large family {{taxfmt|Gobiidae|family}}, in which the [[pelvic fin]]s are fused to form a disc-shaped sucker.
# A [[gudgeon]] of fish of the subfamily {{taxfmt|Gobioninae|subfamily}}, such as {{taxfmt|Gobio gobio|species}}.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1966|title=Oceanology|page=321
|text=For acclimatization in the Barents Sea he recommends using the fish fauna of East Kamchatka and the Bering Sea, especially the Atka mackerel, the '''Goby''' ''Gobio gobio lepidolaemus'' (half scaled goby) and a species of flatfish, in the{{nb...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1980|author=Erik Carp|title=Directory of Wetlands of International Importance in the Western Palearctic|publisher=IUCN|isbn=9782880323004|page=70
|text=Other fish species include Barbel ''Barbus barbus'', '''Goby''' ''Gobio gobio'', Minnow ''Phoxinus phoxinus'', Dace ''Leuciscus leuciscus'', Chub ''Leuciscus cephalus'', Ide ''Leuciscus idus'', Nase ''Chondrostona nasus'', Burbot ''Lota lota'', Pike ''Esox lucius''{{nb...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1997|title=Journal of Ichthyology|page=463
|text=[...] undermonth ''Chondrostoma nasus'', bleak ''Alburnus alburnus'', '''goby''' ''Gobio gobio'', pine ''Esox lucius'', perch ''Perca fluviatilis'', ruffe ''Gymnocephalus cernuus'', spiny loach ''Cobitis taenia'', stone loach ''Nemacheilus barbatulus'', sculpin ''Cottus gobio'', and burbot ''Lota lota'' (Pavlov ''et al.'', 1981).}}

